{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NxDrhLaRkTAukSvaEenFJz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Working notes\n2\t\n3\t## Emoji data and search\n4\t\n5\t- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n6\t  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n7\t- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n8\t  substring, then keyword prefix.\n9\t- The JSON dataset import uses `with { type: 'json' }`. The tsconfig\n10\t  module must be `ESNext` (or `NodeNext`/`Preserve`) to accept import\n11\t  attributes. esbuild preserves the attribute in ESM output and lowers\n12\t  it to `require` in CJS output.\n13\t- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n14\t  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n15\t\n16\t## Picker component conventions\n17\t\n18\t- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n19\t  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n20\t- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n21\t  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n22\t- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n23\t  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n24\t\n25\t## Component exports\n26\t\n27\t- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n28\t  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n29\t- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n30\t  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n31\t- `test/smoke.mjs` runs in Node after build and before the browser bundle.\n32\t  It verifies ESM and CJS loading of every subpath. Extend it when adding\n33\t  new subpaths or CSS export entries.\n34\t## Picker state and interaction\n35\t\n36\t- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n37\t  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n38\t- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n39\t  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n40\t\n41\t## Placement helper\n42\t\n43\t- `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and\n44\t  picker for positioning popovers relative to an anchor. It must not\n45\t  reference `document` or `window` at import time so it stays safe for\n46\t  Node imports.\n47\t- Unit tests for placement live in `test/placement.ts` and run in Node\n48\t  via esbuild bundling (no browser needed).\n49\t- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n50\t  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n51\t  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n52\t- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n53\t  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n54\t  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n55\t  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n56\t  behavior.\n57\t- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n58\t  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n59\t  controls should follow this dispatch pattern.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6bde644-44ab-498a-8659-5687eac90585","uuid":"fa79ebcb-0bab-43f7-af91-3c6f645c85e9","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:46:53.349Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-04-css-subpaths-and-package-metadata/AGENTS.md","content":"# Working notes\n\n## Emoji data and search\n\n- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n  substring, then keyword prefix.\n- The JSON dataset import uses `with { type: 'json' }`. The tsconfig\n  module must be `ESNext` (or `NodeNext`/`Preserve`) to accept import\n  attributes. esbuild preserves the attribute in ESM output and lowers\n  it to `require` in CJS output.\n- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n\n## Picker component conventions\n\n- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n\n## Component exports\n\n- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n- `test/smoke.mjs` runs in Node after build and before the browser bundle.\n  It verifies ESM and CJS loading of every subpath. Extend it when adding\n  new subpaths or CSS export entries.\n## Picker state and interaction\n\n- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n\n## Placement helper\n\n- `src/placement.ts` is a pure function shared by the autocomplete and\n  picker for positioning popovers relative to an anchor. It must not\n  reference `document` or `window` at import time so it stays safe for\n  Node imports.\n- Unit tests for placement live in `test/placement.ts` and run in Node\n  via esbuild bundling (no browser needed).\n- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n  behavior.\n- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n  controls should follow this dispatch pattern.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
